2)	Tell me about some of the responsibilities that you do at home. What are your responsibilities? 
  How often do you do them? What steps do you take to get them done?
  
3)	Think back to your childhood. I would like to know about your responsibilities at home when you were a child.
What were your responsibilities? Tell me everything you remember.
  
4)	Tell me about an issue or a problem you had while getting your responsibilities done. What was the problem?
  How did you solve the issue? Describe your experience in detail.
  
5)	You indicated in the survey that you like to go to the beach. Tell me about a beach you especially like to go.
  Tell me how you get there from your place and what activities you enjoy there.

6)	What kind of activities do people enjoy at the beach? Give me a detailed description about the kinds of 
activities people like to do at the beach.
  
7)	When was the last time you went to a beach? What kind of activities did you do there? Who were you with? 
  Tell me about your last trip with as many details as you can.

8)	Describe to me about the weather of each season in your country. What is the weather like in each season?
  How do you deal with each season?
  
9)	How do you think has the weather changed in each season? Compared to the past what has changed? 
  What stays the same? Tell me in detail.
  
10)	Tell me about a memorable experience you had regarding the weather. Maybe there was heavy rain or snowfall.
  Tell me about all the things you remember about that day.
  
11)	There is a swimming pool you want to go to during your holiday. Call the swimming pool and ask 3 or 4 
  questions about using their facility.
  
12)	You noticed a child playing in a deep pool all by himself without a parent or a guardian. Explain this
  situation to a staff in the swimming pool and provide 2 or 3 suggestions.
  
13)	Tell me about one of your memorable or unforgettable experiences that happened in a swimming pool. 
  What happened? Why was it so unforgettable to you? Tell me in detail.

14)	How has the style of homes changed over the past 5 or 10 years at where you live? Are the homes being built
today different from the homes built 10 years ago? What developments or changes have you noticed?
  
15)	Sometimes issues of too many new homes or not enough new homes can create a controversy in a community. 
  Think of a time when the issue regarding housing was in the news in your area. What was the issue and 
why were people talking about it?
